From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noxwell <beebono@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 08:40:57 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 125/225] arm64: sprd: ums512: port audio
 (VBC/MCDT/AUDCP/codec) plumbing to 7.1

Carries the 6.16 ums512 audio bring-up forward: vbc-v4-dsp.c/.h,
ums9230-digital.c, sprd-mcdt.c, and ums9230-card.c wholesale (SDM init,
mux_dac_out/IIS-master kcontrols, clk_bulk + pm_runtime supply-event fix,
r1p0 MCDT compat, FE_VOICE dailink), with two real API-drift fixes
(snd_soc_dapm_kcontrol_dapm rename, dropped the removed hw_channels
field). sc2730.c and sprd-pcm-dma.c need no changes upstream already
matches or supersedes ours; do NOT re-add the AUDIF soft-reset (upstream
tried and dropped it independently). sprd-audcp-boot.c was missing
entirely upstream and is ported wholesale + Kconfig/Makefile.

DT: agdsp/audcp_boot/vbc/sprd_pcm top-level nodes and
mailbox/mcdt/agcp_dma/dig_codec SoC nodes added to ums512.dtsi, with
memory-region left as a board override (mirrors the &gpu/mali-supply
split) so the generic ums512-1h10.dtb without a reserved-memory
carveout still builds. Board dts gains the four audio reserved-memory
regions, the i2c2 speaker amp, sc2730_codec, and the sound card.

The speaker amp uses upstream's new "anbernic,rgds-amp" compatible
(aw87390.c) instead of porting the old 6.16 aw87391.c shim - upstream
added a match_data variant with the exact register sequence this
handheld's amp needs, driven over i2c with no enable-gpios.

Image + both dtbs build clean and the board boots without a panic.
Flash-tested but not yet audio-tested; the DAC-not-clocked bug from
6.16 is unchanged, only the platform moved (docs/REBASE-7.1-SURVEY.md).
